---

quaydoc is a single Python package with no dependencies beyond the standard
library. Python 3.9 or newer is required.

## Install from source

```console
$ git clone https://example.invalid/quaydoc && cd quaydoc
$ python3 -m quaydoc.cli --version
quaydoc 0.9.0
```

There is nothing to install to try it: run the CLI with
`python3 -m quaydoc.cli` straight from the checkout. To install it into
your environment, use `pip install .` (the project metadata is in
`pyproject.toml`); that also puts a `quaydoc` console script on your path.

## Verify the install

The test suite exercises the lexer, parser, inline markup, slug and anchor
logic, link resolution, the table of contents, the renderers, the template
engine, config loading, the search index, the checker and the CLI:

```console
$ python3 -m pytest -q tests
```

## Supported platforms

quaydoc runs anywhere a current CPython is available and its standard
library is complete.

### Linux & macOS

Both operating systems are supported out of the box; the package has no
platform-specific code and no compiled extensions.

### FAQ: install location

With `pip install .` the package lands in your environment's
`site-packages`; running the CLI directly from the checkout needs no
installation at all.

